        {
          "id": 1221943593,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "The value field is only in the upper four bits of the byte hence the mask. From my understanding the trailing zeroes in the mask are used to shift the integer value to the right (proto.c line ~5568) and then check against the values.\nMaybe a alternative approach would be to use proto_tree_add_bits_item here also sorting out the bits while reading, however I got the feeling that in cases like this there is no real this or that.",
          "author": {
            "id": 9874945,
