      "title": "DECT-NWK: Fix possible overflow",
      "message": "DECT-NWK: Fix possible overflow\n\nCalculating ipei_digits happened using signed int arithmetic due to type\npromotion rules. Explicitely casting the static number to guint64\nensures usage of unsigned 64bit arithmetics.\n",
      "author_name": "Bernhard Dick",
      "author_email": "bernhard@bdick.de",
      "authored_date": "2022-12-23T17:14:35.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
      "committer_email": "a.broman58@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2023-01-02T12:21:44.000+00:00",
      "trailers": {},
      "extended_trailers": {},
      "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/commit/bf7be8a1ae57eac3f703443907051518e0b98ae4"
    },
    {
      "id": "12591d0a42bb06aca52f611bb130c330ad7974d7",
      "short_id": "12591d0a",
      "created_at": "2023-01-02T12:21:44.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "659b830aef88753d7b1ba67230d30add31f7d24e"
      ],
      "title": "DECT-NWK: Fix ELI type decoding",
      "message": "DECT-NWK: Fix ELI type decoding\n\nThe extended location information type field is a four bit value. This\nwas handled correctly while displaying, but not by interpreting the\nvalue. Hence the according MASK and SHIFT values have been updated.\n",
      "author_name": "Bernhard Dick",
      "author_email": "bernhard@bdick.de",
      "authored_date": "2022-12-23T15:27:11.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "AndersBroman",
